Z||000000||Roy Grooms||08-19-2001||11:26 AM|||| I do not have a e- brake  84 2m4 auto trans<BR>i put new calbs ,pads lines on all four,I want to be sure the rear are adjusted right and i can,t recall how to turn the bolt on the calb, to snug the pads up clock or counter. <BR> thanks Roystoy 84 2m4||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-19-2001||11:56 AM||||You don't rotate the bolt. and if the hand brake arms are missing off the caliper, you will have problems.<P>If you aren't very careful playing with manual adjustment of the rear caliper you will drag the pads.<P>Try stepping in the brakes and then rock the lever on the caliper with big pliers. That should knock out the big slop. make sure the brakes don't drag afterwards. You sould see an obvious gap between the inner pad and rotor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Roy Grooms||08-19-2001||01:41 PM|||| Great! now i recall thanks its been a long time seen i did it . ya rock it back and fourth when the brake padel is down, ya the new calbs did not come with the arms and i didntt take the old ones off, don't have an e brake cables were cut and removed when i got the car 4 years ago. had no problems but <BR>had to hand adjust them once, it works but you have to be very carefull not to over tighten them  Great  thanks i must be getting old||||reg||1
